## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, scalable streaming pipeline with multi-region resilience, per-tenant isolation, and strong data governance.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region BigQuery with per-tenant isolation
- Dataflow transforms + DLP-based masking/tokenization
- Data Catalog for lineage and data contracts versioning
- 24h per-tenant rollback via snapshots
- Schema evolution handling and drift alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// High-level pseudo orchestrator (conceptual only)
function flow(tenantId, event) {
  const masked = mask(event, tenantId);
  writeToBigQuery(masked, { tenant: tenantId, region: selectRegion(tenantId) });
  logLineage(tenantId, event, masked);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement schema evolution without breaking tenants?
- How would you test rollback correctness under peak load?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical observability and data reliability skills in a real-world, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Beam Metrics and Cloud Monitoring integration
- Idempotent streaming writes with insertId
- Lightweight auditing and error handling
- Alerting on data quality metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-beam sketch (JavaScript/TypeScript syntax used for illustration)
class ParseEvent extends DoFn {
  @ProcessElement
  process(@Element json, output) {
    const event = JSON.parse(json.image);
    this.ingested.inc();
    // ... validation and transformation
    this.processed.inc();
    output(event);
  }

  @Setup
  setup() {
    this.ingested = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'ingested_events');
    this.processed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'processed_events');
    this.failed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'failed_events');
  }
}
```
